WEBVTT

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:04.230
<b>Jackal</b>

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:04.230
<b>Comics

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:04.230
<b>10,000 
volumes</b>

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:01.190
Two, four, six, eight, ten...

00:02:01.190 --> 00:02:03.810
Two, four, six, eight, ten...

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:06.560
I suppose that's enough.

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:09.560
Thank you very much!

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:15.110
Those "ATMs" sure are 
convenient, though.

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:17.980
You can get money from anywhere.

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:19.870
When I get back, I'll have to have

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:22.700
them set up all throughout my territory.

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:34.840
Hey!

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:36.600
What are you doing?!

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:39.400
Hand over my popsicle!

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:57.760
Jeez. If you're hungry, 
you should've said so.

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:00.120
Sorry, sorry.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:02.550
I haven't had a good meal in days.

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:04.160
I can't tell what you're saying.

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:07.160
That was great.

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:08.840
Thanks.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:11.900
It's so nice of you to buy
 lunch for a stranger.

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:13.160
I'm Ageha.

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:14.300
Who're you?

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:15.580
Nobunaga.

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:17.790
Sweet Little Devil, King Oda Nobunaga.

00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:19.670
Nobunaga, huh?

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:22.180
Okay, nice to meet you Nobucchi!

00:03:23.210 --> 00:03:24.750
Nobucchi?

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:27.960
I was born in the middle of nowhere.

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:30.730
There really was nothing there.

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:33.230
There was no place to hang out.

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:36.450
The only place to go was the 
local convenience store.

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:40.240
And everybody there was just 
so stuck in their ways.

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:43.250
So, I decided that it 
wouldn't do for me at all!

00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:46.450
I'd become a small person if I 
stayed in a place like that!

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:52.340
You know, humans have to 
have big dreams and hopes.

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:56.480
And so I came to the city 
to make my fortune.

00:03:56.480 --> 00:03:59.000
Right now, I'm just living 
in a net cafe all day.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.340
But I've got big dreams of conquest!

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:03.340
Conquest?

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:08.260
But you know, I don't really 
have a goal or anything.

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:10.510
What's this girl's deal?

00:04:10.510 --> 00:04:12.880
She's saying the weirdest things.

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:15.320
So what's your dream, Nobucchi?

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:18.250
My dream? Well, it's of course...

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:22.360
Hey, you kind of stink.

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:24.390
Do I?

00:04:26.420 --> 00:04:29.450
Maybe I do a little.

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:31.420
Sorry, sorry.

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:33.410
I haven't washed these 
clothes in a while.

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:37.210
What is this place?

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:41.210
You've never used a coin 
laundry before, Nobucchi?

00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:44.340
A coin... what?

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:47.490
What are you doing?!

00:04:48.710 --> 00:04:51.180
Put that in an open washing machine.

00:04:54.280 --> 00:04:55.590
Money.

00:04:55.590 --> 00:04:56.840
Why do I have to pay?

00:04:56.840 --> 00:05:00.490
Well, I'm washing it
because you said I smelled!

00:05:00.490 --> 00:05:02.830
You should pay, of course.

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:07.240
Well, maybe...

00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:10.800
You've got a ton of cash!

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:11.870
What's all that for?

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:14.240
Saruko gave it to me.

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:15.360
Saruko?

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:17.130
Is that a friend of yours?

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:19.620
Saruko... Hideyoshi is my retainer.

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:21.130
Not a friend.

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:23.360
Not a friend?

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:26.130
Poor Nobucchi!

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:28.140
You don't have any friends!

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:30.230
Why do you assume that?

00:05:30.230 --> 00:05:32.250
I've got friends!

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:33.320
You do?

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:34.670
Like who?

00:05:34.670 --> 00:05:36.100
Who?

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:37.560
It doesn't matter, does it?

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:43.470
It doesn't...

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:45.860
It doesn't concern you.

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:54.580
What are you doing?

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:56.590
You didn't know, Nobucchi?

00:05:56.590 --> 00:06:00.220
There's money hidden 
under vending machines.

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:04.550
It doesn't have to be 
500, or even 100 yen!

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:08.010
At least a 50 or a 10 yen coin would be...

00:06:08.450 --> 00:06:10.030
I've got something!

00:06:10.030 --> 00:06:12.180
Paper money?

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:16.140
<b>Raffle Ticket</b>

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:20.020
So you give them this and they 
let you enter into a raffle?

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:21.240
Right.

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:23.700
I'll give it to you 
as thanks for lunch,

00:06:23.700 --> 00:06:25.130
so give it a try!

00:06:25.130 --> 00:06:28.070
I'm not interested. I'll pass.

00:06:29.290 --> 00:06:31.520
So you're running, Nobucchi.

00:06:32.270 --> 00:06:34.420
Well, raffles are all about luck.

00:06:34.420 --> 00:06:37.570
And you look like you don't have any.

00:06:37.570 --> 00:06:40.160
If you don't think you can get 
something better than me,

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:41.090
you don't have to do it.

00:06:41.090 --> 00:06:42.000
Fine.

00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:45.050
I'll do it!

00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:48.050
<b>Raffle Booth</b>

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:47.190
Okay, one for each of you.

00:06:47.190 --> 00:06:48.050
Go ahead.

00:06:54.720 --> 00:07:00.310
<b>First Prize   Second Prize  Third Prize   Fourth Prize    Fifth Prize
32-inch          High Class        26-inch         Detergent              Toilet
Plasma               Steak                 ...                                             Paper
...                      Gift Set</b>

00:06:56.340 --> 00:07:00.310
Second prize! High class steak gift set!

00:07:00.860 --> 00:07:02.060
How about that?

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:11.850
Now!

00:07:20.950 --> 00:07:23.000
There it is! Grand prize!

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:26.100
Three days and two nights at a hot springs!

00:07:23.020 --> 00:07:28.780
<b>Grand Prize: Hot Springs Trip</b>

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:28.800
Congratulations!

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:31.530
All right!

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:49.760
I was sure if I watched Ieyasu,

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:52.380
I could find Nobunaga, but...

00:07:52.380 --> 00:07:54.850
Looks like I was wrong.

00:07:57.180 --> 00:07:58.730
Curse you, Nobunaga.

00:07:58.730 --> 00:08:00.330
Where are you?

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:07.750
Yoshimoto-sama, 
this is Sugitani Zenjibo.

00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:11.000
So, you're the famous assassin.

00:08:11.930 --> 00:08:15.600
Using a special gun created 
by Koga ninja techniques,

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:18.470
she never misses.

00:08:19.090 --> 00:08:21.000
Her eyes are sharper than a hawk's,

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:23.790
and she can see farther than any man.

00:08:23.790 --> 00:08:27.220
She never loses a target 
once they're in her sight.

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:29.260
Zenjibo, was it?

00:08:29.260 --> 00:08:29.980
Yes?

00:08:29.980 --> 00:08:32.490
Can you kill Nobunaga?

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:35.490
If that is your command.

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:41.000
Zenjibo, assassinate Nobunaga.

00:08:41.690 --> 00:08:45.820
If you can, you'll have 
whatever reward you like.

00:08:49.990 --> 00:08:54.100
<i>I know that even if I were to 
kill Nobunaga in this world,</i>

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:56.510
<i>I've no hope of getting a reward.</i>

00:08:57.010 --> 00:09:01.270
<i>But, I've endured harsh training as 
an assassin since I was little.</i>

00:09:02.660 --> 00:09:03.310
<i>Endured...</i>

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:05.560
<i>Endured...</i>

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:08.690
<i>Endured!</i>

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:14.860
<i>Even in this strange world, 
this is the only way of life for me.</i>

00:09:15.830 --> 00:09:17.850
<i>It's the only way I can be me.</i>

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:20.870
<i>I'm going to kill Nobunaga.</i>

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:26.370
<b>Uesugi Kenshin</b>

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:28.380
If Ieyasu doesn't work, I can try here.

00:09:28.890 --> 00:09:32.290
Of course, I can't imagine 
Nobunaga would want

00:09:32.290 --> 00:09:34.160
to be anywhere near Kenshin.

00:09:40.110 --> 00:09:41.430
Nobunaga?

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:43.540
Hey, hurry it up!

00:09:43.540 --> 00:09:45.930
If you don't hurry, 
the train will leave!

00:09:45.930 --> 00:09:48.520
Wait, Nobucchi!

00:09:54.430 --> 00:09:58.330
Jeez, I wondered what 
was taking you so long.

00:09:58.330 --> 00:10:00.550
You were buying all those lunches?

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:03.050
How many are you going to eat?

00:10:03.050 --> 00:10:04.320
Now, now.

00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:07.660
I won this trip, so no complaining.

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:09.790
Now, let's eat!

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:11.560
We just got on!

00:10:11.560 --> 00:10:12.680
You're eating already?

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:14.480
Yeah. You won't eat?

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:15.550
Sure, I will.

00:10:16.100 --> 00:10:19.270
<i>I can't believe I found 
her in a place like this!</i>

00:10:19.270 --> 00:10:20.550
<i>What luck!</i>

00:10:20.860 --> 00:10:22.870
Let's eat!

00:10:25.290 --> 00:10:27.390
So good!

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:29.290
Give me that!

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:30.650
Hey!

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:32.350
Come on.

00:10:32.350 --> 00:10:34.530
Give back my beef!

00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:36.650
I love beef, too.

00:10:38.130 --> 00:10:39.950
<i>That's Ageha!</i>

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:44.070
<i>Why?</i>

00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:48.300
<i>Why is Ageha with Nobunaga?</i>

00:10:59.670 --> 00:11:02.970
Why is Ageha here?

00:11:03.490 --> 00:11:08.790
<b>Stop</b>

00:11:07.740 --> 00:11:13.270
<i>Ageha was the first person 
I met in this world.</i>

00:11:13.870 --> 00:11:16.030
What happened to you?

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:24.990
Wh-Who are you?

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:27.070
Is this real?

00:11:27.070 --> 00:11:28.160
Amazing

00:11:27.070 --> 00:11:28.160
Hey!

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:30.910
Does it shoot? Does it shoot bullets?

00:11:29.180 --> 00:11:30.910
Don't touch it!

00:11:30.910 --> 00:11:32.460
Stop!

00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:37.120
You two!

00:11:37.120 --> 00:11:38.960
Crap! Run!

00:11:40.020 --> 00:11:41.330
Hey!

00:11:43.860 --> 00:11:46.730
<i>I didn't know anything about 
living in this world,</i>

00:11:46.730 --> 00:11:50.300
<i>but she taught it to me.</i>

00:11:56.640 --> 00:11:59.900
<i>She was so friendly, so irritating,</i>

00:11:59.900 --> 00:12:02.750
<i>so easy-going, so crazy...</i>

00:12:03.350 --> 00:12:05.420
<i>At first I didn't know 
what to think of her.</i>

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:09.160
An assassin?

00:12:09.420 --> 00:12:10.330
Here.

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:14.870
That's kind of cool!

00:12:15.650 --> 00:12:18.830
No matter what your job is, 
you're still Sugicchi.

00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:21.970
Right?

00:12:25.950 --> 00:12:31.780
<i>The next thing I knew, it was just 
natural for me to be with her,</i>

00:12:32.490 --> 00:12:35.570
<i>and I wanted to stay with her forever.</i>

00:12:38.020 --> 00:12:41.790
<i>That's why I disappeared.</i>

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:45.240
<i>I've always lived my life alone.</i>

00:12:45.630 --> 00:12:48.620
<i>And I always will.</i>

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:51.720
<i>An assassin doesn't need friends.</i>

00:12:51.720 --> 00:12:55.020
<i>All they need is a target.</i>

00:12:57.210 --> 00:13:00.280
Oh, Nobucchi, you're so weird.

00:12:57.210 --> 00:13:02.260
<i>So, what is she doing here?</i>

00:13:03.960 --> 00:13:07.560
Hm, this isn't that bad. 
This place looks nice.

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:10.010
<b>Japanese 
Inn
Shindou</b>

00:13:07.560 --> 00:13:08.530
Doesn't it?

00:13:08.530 --> 00:13:10.010
You should thank me.

00:13:15.550 --> 00:13:18.270
It feels kind of like my old world.

00:13:19.650 --> 00:13:21.030
What are you doing?

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:23.340
Why are you taking your clothes off again?

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:24.960
Why?

00:13:24.960 --> 00:13:26.240
You always go straight to the hot springs

00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:27.530
when you go to a place like this, right?

00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:29.870
Oh, right.

00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:31.120
Then, me, too...

00:13:34.740 --> 00:13:36.500
Um, ma'am.

00:13:38.120 --> 00:13:41.500
Could you remove your clothes 
in the changing room?

00:13:43.810 --> 00:13:44.840
Wait!

00:13:45.430 --> 00:13:47.320
I'll be the first in!

00:13:47.320 --> 00:13:50.600
No, I will!

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:56.470
This is wonderful.

00:13:56.910 --> 00:14:00.060
You sound like an old woman.

00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:02.150
What?

00:14:03.890 --> 00:14:06.770
Your boobs make you look like a cow.

00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:08.940
At this height, I'll 
have to aim from above.

00:14:08.940 --> 00:14:11.620
So I'd have to be pretty far away.

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:14.080
Hey, what are you doing here?

00:14:14.400 --> 00:14:17.040
That felt great.

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:21.410
It's got a ping pong table!

00:14:21.410 --> 00:14:22.940
Ping pong?

00:14:22.940 --> 00:14:24.720
You've never played?

00:14:24.720 --> 00:14:26.760
Of course I have!

00:14:28.910 --> 00:14:31.030
Okay, I'll start!

00:14:31.440 --> 00:14:32.050
Go!

00:14:37.630 --> 00:14:40.170
You suck, Nobucchi.

00:14:40.780 --> 00:14:42.750
O-One more time!

00:14:42.750 --> 00:14:43.900
One more!

00:14:44.120 --> 00:14:46.580
Okay, as many times as you like.

00:14:46.580 --> 00:14:48.380
Hurry up and serve.

00:14:48.380 --> 00:14:50.140
Here I go!

00:14:50.140 --> 00:14:51.270
Go!

00:14:55.710 --> 00:14:59.670
I was interrupted back 
there, but from here...

00:15:02.120 --> 00:15:03.260
Well?

00:15:03.260 --> 00:15:05.250
This is easy!

00:15:06.420 --> 00:15:07.920
Not bad, Nobucchi!

00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:12.800
Stop moving!

00:15:16.820 --> 00:15:17.640
Now!

00:15:23.640 --> 00:15:25.110
Got it!

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:31.820
Huh?

00:15:46.180 --> 00:15:47.780
Wow!

00:15:47.780 --> 00:15:49.380
This looks delicious!

00:15:49.640 --> 00:15:52.040
Let's eat!

00:15:52.040 --> 00:15:55.890
For now, I know what she's going to do.

00:15:55.890 --> 00:15:58.150
I'll eat and watch for a while.

00:16:04.520 --> 00:16:06.250
Meat! Meat! Meat!

00:16:06.250 --> 00:16:07.400
It looks great!

00:16:14.230 --> 00:16:15.600
It's so pretty!

00:16:15.600 --> 00:16:17.620
Look at that sashimi!

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:25.520
So big!

00:16:25.520 --> 00:16:26.210
Not gonna talk!

00:16:26.210 --> 00:16:28.380
Not gonna talk while I'm eating this!

00:16:37.790 --> 00:16:39.570
The beach!

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:42.660
Beach, beach, beach!

00:16:42.660 --> 00:16:44.440
Hey, wait!

00:16:47.540 --> 00:16:48.670
Take this!

00:16:54.160 --> 00:16:56.910
Hey! Stop it!

00:16:56.910 --> 00:16:58.660
And take this!

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:03.660
I said stop!

00:17:13.100 --> 00:17:14.310
Jeez...

00:17:18.390 --> 00:17:19.920
What was that?

00:17:19.920 --> 00:17:21.660
Do it again!

00:17:23.010 --> 00:17:27.420
Do it! Do it! Do it! Okay? Please!

00:17:27.420 --> 00:17:28.190
Shut up!

00:17:40.100 --> 00:17:41.490
Nobucchi!

00:17:41.490 --> 00:17:43.630
Do it again!

00:17:41.860 --> 00:17:44.500
What are they doing?

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:25.820
Nobucchi!

00:18:26.700 --> 00:18:28.320
Come here!

00:18:28.320 --> 00:18:29.630
What?

00:18:36.220 --> 00:18:38.260
What was that for?!

00:19:04.110 --> 00:19:06.290
I'm getting pretty hungry.

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:08.710
Yeah. Let's get a snack.

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:10.290
That's a good idea.

00:19:22.540 --> 00:19:26.470
You!

00:19:27.260 --> 00:19:29.810
Why can't my bullets hit you?!

00:19:30.620 --> 00:19:33.270
And what were you doing just now?

00:19:33.270 --> 00:19:34.940
What's your problem?

00:19:34.940 --> 00:19:35.980
Sugicchi?

00:19:38.840 --> 00:19:40.190
Ageha...

00:19:40.690 --> 00:19:42.840
You know her?

00:19:42.840 --> 00:19:45.950
Yeah, she's an assassin named Sugicchi.

00:19:46.270 --> 00:19:47.810
An assassin?

00:19:47.810 --> 00:19:50.000
I see. So that's it.

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:52.500
You fool!

00:19:53.190 --> 00:19:56.730
I, the Sweet Little Devil Nobunaga,
 aim to conquer the whole world.

00:19:56.730 --> 00:20:00.000
You only aim to kill someone.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:01.740
Your bullets can't hit me.

00:20:01.740 --> 00:20:03.010
You there.

00:20:03.010 --> 00:20:04.660
Yes, Nobunaga-sama!

00:20:13.760 --> 00:20:16.410
What? What's this?

00:20:19.100 --> 00:20:21.180
Nobucchi, no!

00:20:21.180 --> 00:20:22.380
Don't worry.

00:20:22.380 --> 00:20:24.410
I won't take her life.

00:20:24.410 --> 00:20:26.950
Your treasure is mine.

00:20:55.350 --> 00:20:58.500
Look at her. She'll catch a cold...

00:20:59.360 --> 00:21:01.950
Nah, Ageha's too stupid to catch a cold.

00:21:08.600 --> 00:21:11.580
You really are something,

00:21:12.120 --> 00:21:15.080
to make the little devil girl do this.

00:21:15.080 --> 00:21:17.600
<b>Japanese 
Inn
Shindou</b>

00:21:18.830 --> 00:21:20.180
You're leaving?

00:21:21.970 --> 00:21:25.450
It kind of throws you off 
your rhythm, being with her.

00:21:25.850 --> 00:21:30.040
She'll be sad if you go.

00:21:30.040 --> 00:21:33.600
Even if I'm gone,
she'll be okay if you stay with her.

00:21:34.170 --> 00:21:36.570
Be a good friend to her.

00:21:36.570 --> 00:21:37.680
I will.

00:21:41.840 --> 00:21:44.450
I'll be her friend...

00:21:53.560 --> 00:21:59.260
That's just so mean of Nobucchi, 
vanishing like that.

00:21:59.260 --> 00:22:02.550
I'm sure she has her reasons.

00:22:02.550 --> 00:22:06.970
But don't you just disappear! Okay?

00:22:07.400 --> 00:22:08.660
Don't ever!

00:22:10.630 --> 00:22:11.570
Yeah.

00:23:45.970 --> 00:23:47.690
Kondou Isami, the Golden Peony.

00:23:47.690 --> 00:23:49.450
Hijikata Toshizou, the Black Bellflower.

00:23:49.450 --> 00:23:51.700
Okita Souji, the White Lotus.

00:23:51.700 --> 00:23:55.520
Next time on Sengoku 
Collection: "Noble Deciders."

